# The analysis toolchain verify.sh and the workflows install, in one place.
#
# Sourced by verify.sh (for the install hint), by .github/workflows/verify.yml
# (`. scripts/tool-versions.env` before every install), and read by
# scripts/verify-lib.test.mjs, which fails when a workflow installs any of them
# from a floating reference. Floating versions made the debt ratchet and the
# nilaway ceiling a measurement of whichever release a run happened to fetch.
#
# Each value is what the tool resolved to when it was pinned (2026-10-10):
# golangci-lint v2.14.0, govulncheck v1.8.0 (database read at run time),
# nilaway at the commit below, cargo-audit 0.22.2, ruff 0.15.20 (bench/ and scripts/*.py lint), rustc 1.99.0, node 22.22.2
# (jsdom 30 requires ^22.22.2; mermaid 12 requires 22.12+). Raise them
# deliberately, in a change that also re-measures manvi/.golangci-debt.counts
# and the nilaway ceiling in verify.sh.
GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION=v2.14.0
GOVULNCHECK_VERSION=v1.8.0
NILAWAY_VERSION=v0.0.0-20260918162853-acb8859b9031
CARGO_AUDIT_VERSION=0.22.2
RUFF_VERSION=0.15.20
RUST_TOOLCHAIN=1.99.0
NODE_VERSION=22.22.2
